From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:16:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/30] drama: the Drama 3 text backbone on CUDA

Drama 3's backbone is a Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-style hybrid: 30 Gated DeltaNet and 10 gated full-attention layers,
each with a 256-expert top-8 block-FP8 MoE and a gated shared expert. Model.run appends rows and returns every
row's final-norm hidden state and the last row's semantic logits.

The kernels follow the arithmetic of the sglang-omni reference: the canonical 64-token chunked GDN prefill
(drama_gdn_chunk.cuh, after flash-linear-attention's kernels as SGLang carries them), the packed recurrent decode,
gated attention with Q/K norm and partial NeoX RoPE, dynamic 1 x 128 FP8 activation quantization, and the BF16
tensor-core GEMMs in drama_backbone_gemm.cu. Weights load as stored; nothing is requantized.

THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md credits flash-linear-attention (MIT), whose chunked kernels the GDN prefill is adapted from
and whose packed decode the recurrence follows.
